You already mentioned all usages I usually apply gems for. Just to confirm
your knowledge and emphasize some usages (I know some more but rarely apply
them, like identifying booze/amethyst by turning the booze to fruit)...

Engraving when you have enough time, e.g. for stashes, or to secure the
up/down-stairs, to save charges of your wand of digging and to have an
engraving that lasts longer than scribbling in the dust.

Throwing identified gems, or at least named gems, at coaligned unicorns to
increase your luck. Throwing gems to pacify unicorns.

Selling of identified gems if you lack some money, e.g. for buying other
stuff or to donate for protection.

I think that are some a couple interesting applications; what else would
you expect them to do? (Mind, there are some other objects with much less
applications; like tinning kits, for example.)

